<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7379" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρπ-αστός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Hec.</u>
			207
		</span></i> &lt;*&gt;lyr. &lt;*&gt;:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>snatched up, carried off,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γίγνεσθαι</span> to be <i>carried
				off,</i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				229c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>carried up the country,</i> i. e. into Central Asia, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γίγνεσθαι πρὸς βασιλέα</span>
			v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.2.33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ποιεῖν τὸν βίον</span> to give
			up his substance <i>as plunder,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				9.26.7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				7.3.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
